MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The assorted heat shrink tubing feels like a useful next purchase because it would help insulate connections made with the crimp terminals I already have.",
    "Adhesives and wiring supplies fit the practical repair needs reflected in my tape, vinyl cement, hose clamps, and connector purchases, even when I would wait for a specific project before buying."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Buffing compound and orange printer filament require projects I have not shown a need for; buying repair supplies does not mean I also polish objects or use a 3D printer.",
    "Threaded pipe plugs do not meet the same need as hose clamps, and replacement test leads would only be useful if they fit equipment I own and need replacing."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in practical tools and repair supplies seems to have been stretched into an interest in almost any workshop activity.",
    "My previous assortment purchases seem to suggest I want more large kits, even though another connector kit could duplicate supplies I already have."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I care about whether a purchase adds something useful to my existing supplies: insulation complements my terminals, while another large terminal assortment may be redundant.",
    "Exact size, equipment compatibility, quantity, and an immediate project matter to me; a particular tubing diameter, ten tubes of glue, or a large caliper can fit my interests without being something I would choose now."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my repair interests but often mistake a related tool or supply for something I currently need."
}
